       97  Lima [ a ] is the capital and largest city of Peru , as well as a primate city . It is located in the valleys of the Chillón , Rímac and Lurín Rivers , in the desert zone of the central coastal part of the country, overlooking the Pacific Ocean. The city is considered the political, cultural, financ
       98  The 2023 census projection indicates that the city of Lima has an estimated population of 10,092,000 inhabitants, making it the second-most populous city in South America after São Paulo and the largest Spanish-speaking city in the world in terms of city proper population. [ 5 ] [ 6 ] The Lima Metro
       99  Lima was named by natives in the agricultural region known by native Peruvians as Limaq . It became the capital and most important city in the Viceroyalty of Peru . Following the Peruvian War of Independence , it became the capital of the Republic of Peru. Around one-third of the national population
      100  As the headquarters of the Andean Community , Lima plays a crucial role in regional diplomacy and trade integration. In October 2013, Lima was chosen to host the 2019 Pan American Games ; these games were held at venues in and around Lima, and were the largest sporting event ever hosted by the count
      102  [ edit ]
